<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fukushima Masanori</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1561">1561</a>–1624</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fukushima Masanori was a Japanese warlord who served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> and fought for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Sekigahara</a> in 1600. Ieyasu rewarded him with Aki and Bingo provinces, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima">Hiroshima</a>. In 1619 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a> stripped him of the domain for repairing Hiroshima Castle without permission, and the Asano family replaced him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fukushima-masanori.jpg" alt="Fukushima Masanori" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Masanori_Fukushima.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
